  "confirmedContract": [
    "Purchase official FAQ: quick-search field > Fn > 설정 > choose up to3 criteria > save; item-name search is possible afterward. Detailed Search(F3) also has an item picker.",
    "Original quick_search_fn adapts menu quick-search actions into header Fn entries. ConfigureQuickSearchCriteriaUserAction opens setup popup and reloads preserving applied search template after its callback.",
    "Original ConfigureQuickSearchCommonProgram distinguishes basic-code autocomplete/picker from slip targets; empty slip targets block a nonempty keyword, and slip targets/value are sent as quick_condition. Server matching semantics remain outside scope.",
    "Criteria candidates come from tenant/business-specific __d$quick_search_setup; company selected property IDs and latest-update/history data are fetched separately. Candidates cannot be inferred from generic UI forms.",
    "Original setting save rejects0 criteria, checks ready/running rebuild queue, sends base_history_record_sid and handles success/cancel/conflict. It saves even unchanged selections. These are static paths, not executed server behavior."
  ],
  "confirmedGap": [
    "Own quick input copies into generic query and applies JSON.stringify(document).includes; there is no Fn settings / selected-targets storage or explicit master-name target resolution.",
    "Existing detailed item reference filter is separate and must remain available; no assumption that it implements configurable quick search."
  ],
